  Home Docs About

  # Terminal browsers

  A terminal browser renders the web into a grid of cells. It is fast over
  slow links, but loses pixel-perfect layout. See the specification for
  details, or read the very long paragraph that follows to check that word
  wrapping preserves link regions across line breaks without losing a single
  word of the text.

  ## Features

  • Links and buttons
  • Nested lists:
      ◦ inner one
      ◦ inner two with a deep link
  • Images: [img: a tiny logo]

